    "text": "Why can a Japanese stock \"stop\" for the day? 🧵\n The Tokyo Stock Exchange caps how far a stock's price can move in one day: the daily price limit (制限値幅). The cap depends on the stock's base price (基準値段), normally the previous day's closing price or final quote.\n Hitting the upper cap is \"stop high\" (ストップ高); hitting the lower cap is \"stop low\" (ストップ安).\n  # Japan    # investing    # TSE    # Financia",
